From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dhiru Kholia <dhiru@openwall.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 11:41:35 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] 9681: Support DWARF type signatures and standalone split
 DWARF

Read DW_FORM_ref_sig8 as an eight-byte type signature and resolve it
through a signature-to-defining-DIE index. Parse DWARF 4 .debug_types
with a virtual combined info stream and recognize DWARF 5 type and split
unit headers. Follow DW_AT_signature from declarations to their type
definitions so imported types and function references use the correct
DIE.

Find standalone .dwo files from skeleton names and compilation
directories, match units by dwo ID, and import the split units into the
program. Borrow address and line sections from the skeleton when needed.
Handle ELF-compressed sections, GNU DWARF 4 indexed addresses and
strings, and headerless offset tables. Report missing, invalid, or
mismatched .dwo files without marking DWARF fully loaded.

Type units may carry DW_AT_stmt_list for declaration file indexes but do
not own executable line mappings. Skip them during source-map import to
avoid replaying line programs for every type unit. Stream decoded rows
into the final list, reuse file paths, and avoid reflection for standard
line opcode names to reduce memory and CPU use.

Add DWARF 4 type-unit and split fixtures, DWARF 5 split and compressed
fixtures, their C++ source, and verified LLVM 23.1.2 reproduction
commands. Certify the six binary fixtures in Base/certification.manifest.

Verification: six focused DWARF tests, :Base:ip, and buildGhidra passed.
A full headless import of an affected ELF completed and saved with Java
27 and a 2 GB heap, adding 120,293 source-map entries.

Scope: standalone .dwo files and type units in the current object or
.dwo. .dwp packages and type references across separate .dwo files are
not covered.
